  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... \nIssued at 227 AM CDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nLittle has changes in the expectations for Friday. The surface \nlow still looks to lift slowly east languishing over Ozarks.  \nThis will allow for additional rounds of showers and storms. \nRainfall amounts from this round remain uncertain as the showery\nnature expected will likely produce widely varying rainfall \namounts across the region. With continued high moisture content \nin the atmosphere, weak mean flow, localized flooding will be a\nconcern, especially with additional rainfall expected for \nSaturday as the low continues its slow progression east. Rain \nchances are lower Saturday than the previous Today or Friday, \nbut the multi-day nature of the rainfall may be enough to begin \ngetting more flooding.\n\nRain chances do begin to taper off slowly Sunday into early \nnext week before the region transitions into a drier pattern by\nWednesday. This will occur as the upper low out west begins to \nlift north into the northern plains. This will bring rising \nheights and decreasing rain chances for the area and would \nsupport warming middle level, 850mb temperatures and warmer \nsurface temperatures for the middle to later portions of next \nweek.",
